# Backend Architecture

Package root: `cn.timebank`. Single Maven module, Spring Boot 3.4, Java 21 with virtual threads.

## Module Structure

Every business module follows this layout:

```
cn.timebank.<module>/
├── web/            @RestController (HTTP binding only)
├── application/    Service interfaces (public) + ServiceImpl (package-private)
│   └── dto/        Request/response Java records
├── domain/         JPA entities, enums, state machines
└── infrastructure/ JpaRepository interfaces
```

Cross-cutting: `cn.timebank.common.*` (envelope, errors, pagination, idempotency, i18n), `cn.timebank.security` (auth, CSRF, data scope).

## Hard Rules

- **Every controller method has `@PreAuthorize`** — ArchUnit enforces this
- **Return `ApiResponse<T>`, never bare entities or ResponseEntity** — contract envelope
- **Entities stay in their owning module** — cross-module reads go through the application service interface
- **No `@Entity` in controllers** — ArchUnit enforces this
- **`@Transactional` lives on services, not controllers**
- **Read-only transactions for queries:** `@Transactional(readOnly = true)`
- **Status changes via state machines** — `XxxStateMachine.canTransition()`, never `if (status == …)` scattered in services
- **Append-only for audit, reviews, transactions** — no update/delete methods on those repositories
- **Multi-module atomic writes use `*Transaction` beans** (e.g. `ReviewDecisionTransaction`) — called through Spring proxy to avoid self-invocation pitfalls

## Naming Conventions

| Element | Convention |
|---------|-----------|
| IDs | Opaque 32-char strings via `OpaqueIds`, `VARCHAR(32)` |
| API paths | `/api/v1/<resource>` (kebab-case) |
| Permissions | dot-separated: `serviceRecords.read`, `users.create` |
| Status enums | Java enum, `@Enumerated(EnumType.STRING)` |
| Tests | `FooTest` (unit/Surefire) vs `FooIT` (integration/Failsafe) |
| DTOs | Java `record` types with Jakarta validation annotations |

## Testing

- `mvn test` — MockMvc slices + ArchUnit (no external deps)
- `mvn verify` — `*IT` classes against real MySQL on test server
- All `*IT` extend `AbstractIntegrationTest` (random port, per-class schema via `MySqlTestSchemaExtension`)
- Needs env vars: `TIMEBANK_DB_HOST`, `TIMEBANK_DB_USERNAME`, `TIMEBANK_DB_PASSWORD`
- **No Docker, no Testcontainers**

## Key Patterns

- `VersionedEntity` base class → `@Version` for optimistic locking
- `ConcurrencyControl.checkVersion()` before writes
- `IdempotencyService.execute()` wraps ledger-affecting mutations
- `AuditService` called inside the business transaction
- Data scope: `DataScopeResolver` → `Specification` filters → 404-not-403 pattern
- Caffeine cache for dictionaries/rules (60s TTL)
- ShedLock for scheduled jobs across instances

## Build

```bash
cd backend
JAVA_HOME=/opt/homebrew/opt/openjdk@21 mvn compile
JAVA_HOME=/opt/homebrew/opt/openjdk@21 mvn test
```
